msgid "LOOP_HELP"
msgstr "A measure is a small group of beats between vertical lines. Repeat a few measures to practice a short phrase."

msgid "HELP_STRINGS"
msgstr "1. Follow the six tab lines. The top line is string 1: your thinnest guitar string."

msgid "HELP_FRETS"
msgstr "2. Press the fret number shown. A 0 means play the open string, without pressing a fret."

msgid "HELP_STAFF"
msgstr "3. The smaller staff above is a pitch and rhythm reference. Higher notes mean higher pitches. Guitar staff notes are written one octave above their sound."

msgid "HELP_TIMING"
msgstr "4. Press Play and count with the clicks. Point at the music to preview a position, or click/tap to seek there. Outlined numbers show sounding notes. A ! means a note has no guitar placement. Slow down with Playback or repeat a phrase with Loop."

msgid "FOLLOW_HINT"
msgstr "Follow the outlined fret numbers."

